intro="Food, fuel, fabrics, medicines and living bodies are all built from carbon compounds, although carbon forms only a small part of the Earth's crust. Carbon's special ability to form long chains, rings and strong bonds explains the huge variety. This chapter covers covalent bonding, the types of carbon chains, naming of organic compounds, the chemistry of ethanol and ethanoic acid, and the cleansing action of soaps and detergents.",
