("p", "Carbon (atomic number 6, electronic configuration 2,4) has four valence electrons. Losing four electrons needs too much energy, and gaining four is difficult for a small nucleus, so carbon **shares** electrons. Sharing a pair of electrons forms a **covalent bond**. In methane CH<sub>4</sub>, carbon shares one pair with each of four hydrogens; in O<sub>2</sub> two pairs are shared (double bond); N<sub>2</sub> shares three pairs (triple bond)."),
