("p", "**Structural isomers:** compounds with the same molecular formula but different structures. Butane C<sub>4</sub>H<sub>10</sub> has two: straight-chain butane and branched 2-methylpropane. Rings such as cyclohexane C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>12</sub> and benzene C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>6</sub> also exist."),
("h2", "4.3 Functional Groups, Homologous Series and Nomenclature"),
("note", "DEFINITION", "A **functional group** is an atom or group of atoms that decides the chemical properties of a compound. A **homologous series** is a family of compounds with the same functional group, the same general formula and similar chemical properties; consecutive members differ by **&ndash;CH<sub>2</sub>&ndash;** (14 u)."),
